      "durationSeconds": 55.04,
      "transcript": "Kosanchychov Overlook Belgrade first becomes a city on an edge above water. Come to the edge and first look down, not out for famous objects. The city changes shape here. What was just an old center becomes the rim of a high plateau. The Sava is not beside you, it is below you. This overlook is still urban, with cobbles, houses and quiet courtyards, but it works like a balcony over the river. Here it becomes easier to understand Old Belgrade as a city held above the water, Protected by height yet always pulled downward to docks, cargo and river work. The sharp drop between street and river, the Sava below rather than beside you. Old houses almost on the plateau edge. Choose a spot where you can see both slope and river, not only the far horizon. This is a good short pause before the fortress. Walk toward Kalamegden and Sahat Gate. After the open edge, you enter the place where terrain became defense.",
